SMTP_USER=your.email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASSWORD=your_gmail_app_password
```

#### [NEW] `backend/app/core/email.py`
New email service module:
- `send_verification_email(to_email, token)` — sends a verification link
- `send_password_reset_email(to_email, token)` — sends a reset link
- Uses Python's built-in `smtplib` + `email.mime` (no extra dependencies needed)
- Generates clean HTML emails with the app branding

#### [MODIFY] [models.py](file:///e:/Projects/FYP-PROJECT-UPDATED/fyp_SLM-/backend/app/models.py) — User model
Add one new column:
```python
is_email_verified = Column(Boolean, default=False)
```

#### [NEW] Alembic migration
Add `is_email_verified` column to `users` table.

#### [MODIFY] [auth.py](file:///e:/Projects/FYP-PROJECT-UPDATED/fyp_SLM-/backend/app/routers/auth.py)
- **`POST /register`**: After creating the user, generate a verification token (UUID4), store it in Redis with 24-hour TTL, and send the verification email. User is created with `is_email_verified=False`.
- **`GET /verify-email?token=...`** (NEW): Validates the token against Redis, sets `is_email_verified=True`, deletes the token.
- **`POST /resend-verification`** (NEW): If user hasn't verified yet, generates a new token and re-sends the email. Rate-limited to 1 per 60 seconds per email (stored in Redis).

#### Access Control: Hard Gate (Login Blocked)

Unverified users **cannot log in**. The login endpoint will check `is_email_verified` after password validation and return:
```python
raise HTTPException(
    status_code=403,
    detail={"field": "email", "message": "Please verify your email before logging in. Check your inbox for the verification link.", "action": "resend_verification"}
)
```
The frontend login form will detect `action: "resend_verification"` and show a "Resend verification email" button inline, so the user is never stuck.

#### [NEW] `frontend/app/verify-email/page.tsx`
- Landing page when user clicks the email link
- Calls `GET /auth/verify-email?token=...`
- Shows success → redirects to `/login`
- Shows error if token is expired/invalid → offers "Resend verification email" button

#### [MODIFY] [SignupForm.tsx](file:///e:/Projects/FYP-PROJECT-UPDATED/fyp_SLM-/frontend/components/forms/SignupForm.tsx)
- After successful registration, **do NOT auto-login** (login will be blocked anyway since email is unverified)
- Redirect to a "Check your email" interstitial page with the message: *"We've sent a verification link to your email. Please verify before logging in."*
- Include a "Resend email" button and a "Back to login" link

