## 3. Forgot Password / Reset Password (Gmail SMTP)

### How It Works

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant FE as Frontend
    participant BE as FastAPI
    participant GM as Gmail SMTP
    participant R as Redis

    U->>FE: Clicks "Forgot password?" on login page
    FE->>FE: Show forgot password form
    U->>FE: Enters email, clicks "Send Reset Link"
    FE->>BE: POST /auth/forgot-password {email}
    BE->>BE: Look up user by email
    BE->>R: Store reset token → user_id (TTL: 15 min)
    BE->>GM: Send email with reset link
    GM->>U: Email: "Click to reset your password"
    BE->>FE: 200 OK (always — even if email not found)
    FE->>FE: Show "Check your email" message

    U->>FE: Clicks link in email
    FE->>FE: Show reset password form
    U->>FE: Enters new password + confirm
    FE->>BE: POST /auth/reset-password {token, new_password}
    BE->>R: Validate token → user_id
    BE->>BE: Hash new password, update user
    BE->>R: Delete token (single-use)
    BE->>FE: 200 OK
    FE->>FE: Redirect to /login with success message
```

### Security Measures

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **Anti-enumeration**: `POST /forgot-password` ALWAYS returns `200 OK` with `"If an account exists with this email, a reset link has been sent."` — even if no user exists. This prevents attackers from discovering valid email addresses.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **Rate limiting**: Maximum 3 reset requests per email per hour (tracked in Redis). Prevents email flooding.

> [!IMPORTANT]  
> **Single-use tokens**: Each reset token is deleted from Redis after use. Clicking the link twice won't work.

### Proposed Changes

#### [MODIFY] [auth.py](file:///e:/Projects/FYP-PROJECT-UPDATED/fyp_SLM-/backend/app/routers/auth.py)
- **`POST /forgot-password`** (NEW): Accepts `{email}`. If user exists, generates a reset token (UUID4), stores in Redis (15-min TTL), sends reset email. Always returns success.
- **`POST /reset-password`** (NEW): Accepts `{token, new_password}`. Validates token against Redis, hashes new password, updates user, deletes token.

#### [NEW] `frontend/app/forgot-password/page.tsx`
- Simple form: email input + "Send Reset Link" button
- On success: shows *"If an account exists with this email, a reset link has been sent. Check your inbox."*
- Link back to login page

#### [NEW] `frontend/app/reset-password/page.tsx`
- Reads `?token=...` from URL
- Form: new password + confirm password (with same validation rules as signup)
- On success: toast + redirect to `/login`
- On error (expired/invalid token): shows error + link to retry forgot password

